# [CCWG](../wg/ccwg.html)

## Summary

The Congestion Control Working Group (CCWG) met at IETF 127. The session covered progress updates on active working group items, including BBR Congestion Control ([draft-ietf-ccwg-bbr](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-ccwg-bbr/)) and SCReAM v2 ([draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2/)). The working group also received updates from the IETF 127 Hackathon on QUIC NS-3 simulator integrations and L4S interop testing. Finally, individual proposals were presented on Network Delivery Time Control (`draft-nguyen-ccwg-ndtc`), Cuback (`draft-oku-ccwg-cuback`), an analysis of standard congestion control differences (`draft-nishida-ccwg-standard-cc-analysis`), and C4 (`draft-huitema-ccwg-c4`). A working group poll was conducted regarding potential work on updating Reno and/or CUBIC specifications.

